IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`

-- wra2-s46-jsa-sanctions.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK) s 46 (ss 47 and 48), jobseeker's allowance sanctions in the interim period.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part wra2. Host Act short name: JSA = Jobseekers Act 1995.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt (a converter script's plain-text rendering; not the official text).
-- Section 46 substitutes JSA 19 (higher-level sanctions), 19A (other sanctions) and inserts 19B (ceasing to be available)
-- and 19C (hardship payments), and Schedule 1 para 14AA (good reason).
-- Amounts and periods of reductions are left to regulations that are not among the sources, so they are inputs.
-- Mapping to the core's `Provision that reduces an award` (seam 9 of PLAN.md):
--   JSA 19 -> `jobseeker's allowance higher-level sanction`; JSA 19A -> `jobseeker's allowance other sanction`;
--   JSA 19B -> `jobseeker's allowance ceasing to be available`.

§ `s 46 Sanctions: the logic of three-valued answers`

-- Logic only: these three helpers carry the FALSE and NOTHING of their arguments; they add no reading of the Act.
GIVEN `x` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `y` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `x` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `y` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `x` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `y` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `x` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `y` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `x` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `y` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `x` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `y` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `x` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `x` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `x` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 46(3) JSA Schedule 1 paragraph 14AA: good reason`

DECLARE `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason` IS ONE OF
    `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA treated as having a good reason`
    `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA treated as not having a good reason`
    `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations do not address the case`

-- src:676 | 14AA
-- src:677 | For any purpose of this Act regulations may provide for—
-- src:678 | (a) circumstances in which a person is to be treated as having or not having a good reason for an act or omission;
@ref s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) (src:676-678)
GIVEN `the claimant had a good reason on the facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how regulations treat the case` IS A MAYBE `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) the claimant has a good reason for the act or omission` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how regulations treat the case`
    WHEN JUST `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA treated as having a good reason` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "circumstances in which a person is to be treated as having or not having a good reason" -- regulations treat the claimant as not having one
    WHEN JUST `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA treated as not having a good reason` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations do not address the case` THEN JUST `the claimant had a good reason on the facts`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations under paragraph 14AA are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `s 46 JSA 19: higher-level sanctions`

DECLARE `s 46 JSA 19(2) failure` HAS
    `through misconduct the claimant loses employment as an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant voluntarily leaves such employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a situation in employment that an employment officer has informed the claimant is vacant or about to become vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant neglects to avail of a reasonable opportunity of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant fails to participate in a scheme within section 17A(1) prescribed for the purposes of section 19` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:584 | (2) It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant—
-- src:585 | (a) through misconduct loses employment as an employed earner;
-- src:586 | (b) without a good reason voluntarily leaves such employment;
-- src:587 | (c) without a good reason refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a situation in any employment which an employment officer has informed him is vacant or about to become vacant;
-- src:588 | (d) without a good reason neglects to avail himself of a reasonable opportunity of employment;
-- src:589 | (e) without a good reason fails to participate in any scheme within section 17A(1) which is prescribed for the purposes of this section.
-- src:590 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)(b), in such circumstances as may be prescribed, including in particular where a person has been dismissed by his employer by reason of redundancy within the meaning of section 139(1) of the Employment Rights Act 1996 after volunteering or agreeing to be so dismissed, a person who might otherwise be treated as having left his employment voluntarily is to be treated as not having left voluntarily.
@ref s 46 JSA 19(2) with 19(3) (src:584-590)
GIVEN `the failure` IS A `s 46 JSA 19(2) failure`
      `the claimant had a good reason` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations treat the claimant as not having left the employment voluntarily` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 19` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant -- (a) ... (e)" -- none of the five limbs holds (a failed "if", reading (a) of NOTES)
    `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` (JUST (`the failure`'s `through misconduct the claimant loses employment as an employed earner`))
        (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either`
            (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant voluntarily leaves such employment`))
                (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`)
                                           (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `regulations treat the claimant as not having left the employment voluntarily`)))
            (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either`
                (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a situation in employment that an employment officer has informed the claimant is vacant or about to become vacant`))
                                           (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`))
                (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either`
                    (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant neglects to avail of a reasonable opportunity of employment`))
                                               (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`))
                    (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant fails to participate in a scheme within section 17A(1) prescribed for the purposes of section 19`))
                                               (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`)))))

-- src:583 | (1) The amount of an award of a jobseeker's allowance is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure by the claimant which is sanctionable under this section.
-- src:597 | (6) Regulations may provide—
-- src:598 | (a) for cases in which no reduction is to be made under this section;
@ref s 46 JSA 19(1) with 19(6)(a) (src:583 src:597-598)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 19` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in the case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19(1) the award is to be reduced in accordance with section 19` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure ... which is sanctionable under this section" -- there is no such failure
        IF `the failure is sanctionable under section 19` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the failure is sanctionable under section 19` EQUALS NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether there is a sanctionable failure is not known
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in the case`
            -- FALSE-kind (supplied): regulations under 19(6)(a) provide for cases in which no reduction is to be made
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulations under 19(6)(a) are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:591 | (4) Regulations are to provide for—
-- src:592 | (a) the amount of a reduction under this section;
@ref s 46 JSA 19(4)(a) (src:591-592)
GIVEN `the award before the reduction, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 46 JSA 19(4)(a) the award after the reduction, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds`
    WHEN JUST reduction THEN
        BRANCH
            IF reduction AT MOST `the award before the reduction, in pounds`
            THEN JUST (`the award before the reduction, in pounds` MINUS reduction)
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what happens when the reduction is more than the award
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations are to provide for the amount of a reduction"; they are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:593 | (b) the period for which such a reduction has effect, not exceeding three years in relation to any failure sanctionable under this section.
@ref s 46 JSA 19(4)(b) (src:593)
GIVEN `the first day of the reduction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19(4)(b) the period of the reduction is within three years` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not exceeding three years in relation to any failure sanctionable under this section" -- the last day is after the day before the third anniversary of the first day
    `the last day of the reduction`
        AT MOST (Date (DATE_DAY `the first day of the reduction`) (DATE_MONTH `the first day of the reduction`) (DATE_YEAR `the first day of the reduction` PLUS 3) MINUS 1)

-- src:599 | (b) for a reduction under this section made in relation to an award that is terminated to be applied to any new award made within a prescribed period of the termination.
@ref s 46 JSA 19(6)(b) (src:599)
GIVEN `the earlier award was terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new award was made within the period regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that the reduction is applied to the new award` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19(6)(b) the reduction on the terminated award is applied to the new award` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the earlier award was terminated`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a reduction ... made in relation to an award that is terminated"
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` `regulations provide that the reduction is applied to the new award` `the new award was made within the period regulations prescribe`

DECLARE `s 46 JSA 19(7) the member of the couple` IS ONE OF
    `s 46 JSA 19(7) the first person`
    `s 46 JSA 19(7) the second person`

-- src:600 | (7) During any period for which the amount of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance is reduced under this section by virtue of a failure by one of the claimants which is sanctionable under this section, the allowance is payable to the other member of the couple.
@ref s 46 JSA 19(7) (src:600)
GIVEN `the joint claimants` IS A `Two people`
      `the claimant whose failure it is` IS A `s 46 JSA 19(7) the member of the couple`
      `the allowance is reduced during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Person
`s 46 JSA 19(7) the member of the couple to whom the allowance is payable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the allowance is reduced during the period`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "During any period for which the amount of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance is reduced"
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the claimant whose failure it is`
            WHEN `s 46 JSA 19(7) the first person` THEN JUST (`the joint claimants`'s `the second person`)
            WHEN `s 46 JSA 19(7) the second person` THEN JUST (`the joint claimants`'s `the first person`)

§ `s 46 JSA 19A: other sanctions`

DECLARE `s 46 JSA 19A(2) failure` HAS
    `the claimant fails to comply with regulations under section 8(1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant fails to comply with regulations under section 17A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant refuses or fails to carry out a jobseeker's direction that was reasonable having regard to the claimant's circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant neglects to avail of a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a place on such a scheme or programme that an employment officer has informed the claimant is vacant or about to become vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant gives up a place on such a scheme or programme or fails to attend it having been given a place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `through misconduct the claimant loses a place on such a scheme or programme` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:603 | (2) It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant—
-- src:604 | (a) without a good reason fails to comply with regulations under section 8(1) or (1A);
-- src:605 | (b) without a good reason fails to comply with regulations under section 17A;
-- src:606 | (c) without a good reason refuses or fails to carry out a jobseeker's direction which was reasonable having regard to his circumstances;
-- src:607 | (d) without a good reason neglects to avail himself of a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme;
-- src:608 | (e) without a good reason refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a place on such a scheme or programme which an employment officer has informed him is vacant or about to become vacant;
-- src:609 | (f) without a good reason gives up a place on such a scheme or programme or fails to attend such a scheme or programme having been given a place on it;
-- src:610 | (g) through misconduct loses a place on such a scheme or programme.
@ref s 46 JSA 19A(2) (src:603-610)
GIVEN `the failure` IS A `s 46 JSA 19A(2) failure`
      `the claimant had a good reason` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19A(2) the failure is of a kind that section 19A(2) makes sanctionable` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant -- (a) ... (g)" -- none of the seven limbs holds (a failed "if", reading (a) of NOTES)
    `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either`
        (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant fails to comply with regulations under section 8(1) or (1A)`)) (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`))
        (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either`
            (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant fails to comply with regulations under section 17A`)) (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`))
            (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either`
                (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant refuses or fails to carry out a jobseeker's direction that was reasonable having regard to the claimant's circumstances`)) (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`))
                (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either`
                    (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant neglects to avail of a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme`)) (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`))
                    (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either`
                        (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a place on such a scheme or programme that an employment officer has informed the claimant is vacant or about to become vacant`)) (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`))
                        (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either`
                            (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`the failure`'s `the claimant gives up a place on such a scheme or programme or fails to attend it having been given a place`)) (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`))
                            (JUST (`the failure`'s `through misconduct the claimant loses a place on such a scheme or programme`)))))))

-- src:611 | (3) But a failure is not sanctionable under this section if it is also sanctionable under section 19.
@ref s 46 JSA 19A(3) (src:611)
GIVEN `the failure is of a kind that section 19A(2) makes sanctionable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the failure is also sanctionable under section 19` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19A(3) the failure is sanctionable under section 19A` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But a failure is not sanctionable under this section if it is also sanctionable under section 19"
        IF `the failure is also sanctionable under section 19` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` `the failure is of a kind that section 19A(2) makes sanctionable` (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the failure is also sanctionable under section 19`)

-- src:602 | (1) The amount of an award of a jobseeker's allowance is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure by the claimant which is sanctionable under this section.
-- src:633 | (a) for cases in which no reduction is to be made under this section;
@ref s 46 JSA 19A(1) with 19A(9)(a) (src:602 src:633)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 19A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in the case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19A(1) the award is to be reduced in accordance with section 19A` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure ... which is sanctionable under this section" -- there is no such failure
        IF `the failure is sanctionable under section 19A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the failure is sanctionable under section 19A` EQUALS NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether there is a sanctionable failure is not known
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in the case`
            -- FALSE-kind (supplied): regulations under 19A(9)(a) provide for cases in which no reduction is to be made
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulations under 19A(9)(a) are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:617 | (b) a fixed period not exceeding 26 weeks which is—
@ref s 46 JSA 19A(5)(b) (src:617)
GIVEN `the first day of the reduction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19A(5)(b) the fixed period of the reduction is within 26 weeks` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fixed period not exceeding 26 weeks" -- 26 weeks is 182 days, both days counting
    ((Day `the last day of the reduction` MINUS Day `the first day of the reduction`) PLUS 1) AT MOST 182

DECLARE `s 46 JSA 19A(6) kind of condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 46 JSA 19A(6)(a) a condition that the failure ceases`
    `s 46 JSA 19A(6)(b)(i) a condition relating to future compliance with a jobseeker's direction or a requirement under section 8(1) or (1A) or 17A`
    `s 46 JSA 19A(6)(b)(ii) a condition relating to future avoidance of the failures in subsection (2)(d) to (g)`
    `s 46 JSA 19A(6) some other condition`

-- src:621 | (6) In subsection (5)(a) “compliance condition” means—
-- src:622 | (a) a condition that the failure ceases, or
-- src:623 | (b) a condition relating to—
-- src:624 | (i) future compliance with a jobseeker's direction or any requirement imposed under section 8(1) or (1A) or 17A of this Act, or
-- src:625 | (ii) future avoidance of the failures referred to in subsection (2)(d) to (g).
@ref s 46 JSA 19A(6) (src:621-625)
GIVEN `the condition` IS A `s 46 JSA 19A(6) kind of condition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19A(6) the condition is a compliance condition` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the condition`
    WHEN `s 46 JSA 19A(6)(a) a condition that the failure ceases` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 46 JSA 19A(6)(b)(i) a condition relating to future compliance with a jobseeker's direction or a requirement under section 8(1) or (1A) or 17A` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 46 JSA 19A(6)(b)(ii) a condition relating to future avoidance of the failures in subsection (2)(d) to (g)` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“compliance condition” means" the two kinds listed
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:626 | (7) A compliance condition specified under subsection (5)(a) may be—
-- src:627 | (a) revoked or varied by the Secretary of State;
@ref s 46 JSA 19A(7)(a) (src:626 src:627)
GIVEN `the person who revokes or varies the compliance condition` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19A(7)(a) the compliance condition may be revoked or varied by that person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person who revokes or varies the compliance condition` EQUALS `the Secretary of State`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be revoked or varied by the Secretary of State" says nothing of any other person
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:626 | (7) A compliance condition specified under subsection (5)(a) may be—
-- src:628 | (b) notified to the claimant in such manner as the Secretary of State may determine.
@ref s 46 JSA 19A(7)(b) (src:626 src:628)
GIVEN `the manner of notification is one the Secretary of State has determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19A(7)(b) the compliance condition is notified in a manner the Secretary of State may determine` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the manner of notification is one the Secretary of State has determined`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notified to the claimant in such manner as the Secretary of State may determine" says nothing of a manner the Secretary of State has not determined
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 46 JSA 19A(11) direction` HAS
    `given by an employment officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with a view to assisting the claimant to find employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with a view to improving the claimant's prospects of being employed` IS A BOOLEAN

