`s 46 JSA 19A(11)(b) the scheme is a training scheme or employment programme` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "have such meaning as may be prescribed"; the prescribing regulations are not among the sources
    `the meaning regulations prescribe for the term`

§ `s 46 JSA 19A(10) and 19B(8): joint claims`

-- src:635 | (10) During any period for which the amount of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance is reduced under this section by virtue of a failure by one of the claimants which is sanctionable under this section, the allowance is payable to the other member of the couple.
@ref s 46 JSA 19A(10) (src:635)
GIVEN `the joint claimants` IS A `Two people`
      `the claimant whose failure it is` IS A `s 46 JSA 19(7) the member of the couple`
      `the allowance is reduced during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Person
`s 46 JSA 19A(10) the member of the couple to whom the allowance is payable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the allowance is reduced during the period`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "During any period for which the amount of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance is reduced"
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the claimant whose failure it is`
            WHEN `s 46 JSA 19(7) the first person` THEN JUST (`the joint claimants`'s `the second person`)
            WHEN `s 46 JSA 19(7) the second person` THEN JUST (`the joint claimants`'s `the first person`)

§ `s 46 JSA 19B: claimants ceasing to be available for employment etc`

-- src:642 | (1) Regulations may make provision for reduction of the amount of an award of a jobseeker's allowance other than a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance if the claimant—
-- src:643 | (a) was previously entitled to such an allowance or was a member of a couple entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance, and
-- src:644 | (b) ceased to be so entitled by failing to comply with the condition in section 1(2)(a) or (c) (availability for employment and actively seeking employment).
@ref s 46 JSA 19B(1) (src:642-644)
GIVEN `the award is of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was previously entitled to such an allowance or was a member of a couple entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant ceased to be so entitled by failing to comply with the condition in section 1(2)(a) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19B(1) regulations may provide for a reduction of the award` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     NOT `the award is of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance`
           AND `the claimant was previously entitled to such an allowance or was a member of a couple entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance`
           AND `the claimant ceased to be so entitled by failing to comply with the condition in section 1(2)(a) or (c)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "if the claimant (a) ... and (b) ..." for an award other than a joint-claim allowance; this case is outside it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:645 | (2) Regulations may make provision for reduction of the amount of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance if one of the claimants—
-- src:646 | (a) was previously entitled to a jobseeker's allowance other than a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance, and
-- src:647 | (b) ceased to be so entitled by failing to comply with the condition in section 1(2)(a) or (c).
