GIVEN `the award is of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the claimants was previously entitled to a jobseeker's allowance other than a joint-claim allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that claimant ceased to be so entitled by failing to comply with the condition in section 1(2)(a) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19B(2) regulations may provide for a reduction of the joint-claim award` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the award is of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance`
           AND `one of the claimants was previously entitled to a jobseeker's allowance other than a joint-claim allowance`
           AND `that claimant ceased to be so entitled by failing to comply with the condition in section 1(2)(a) or (c)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given for a joint-claim allowance "if one of the claimants (a) ... and (b) ..."; this case is outside it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:648 | (3) Regulations may make provision for reduction of the amount of an award of joint-claim jobseeker's allowance if—
