-- src:654 | (5) The period referred to in subsection (4)(b) must not include any period after the end of the period of 13 weeks beginning with the day on which the claimant's previous entitlement ceased.
@ref s 46 JSA 19B(5) (src:654)
GIVEN `the day on which the claimant's previous entitlement ceased` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46 JSA 19B(5) the period of the reduction is within 13 weeks of the end of the previous entitlement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not include any period after the end of the period of 13 weeks beginning with the day on which the claimant's previous entitlement ceased" -- 13 weeks is 91 days beginning with that day
    `the last day of the reduction` AT MOST (`the day on which the claimant's previous entitlement ceased` PLUS 90)

-- src:659 | (8) During any period for which the amount of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance is reduced under this section by virtue of a failure by one of the claimants to comply with the condition in section 1(2)(a) or (c), the allowance is payable to the other member of the couple.
@ref s 46 JSA 19B(8) (src:659)
GIVEN `the joint claimants` IS A `Two people`
      `the claimant whose failure it is` IS A `s 46 JSA 19(7) the member of the couple`
      `the allowance is reduced during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Person
`s 46 JSA 19B(8) the member of the couple to whom the allowance is payable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the allowance is reduced during the period`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "During any period for which the amount of a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance is reduced"
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the claimant whose failure it is`
            WHEN `s 46 JSA 19(7) the first person` THEN JUST (`the joint claimants`'s `the second person`)
            WHEN `s 46 JSA 19(7) the second person` THEN JUST (`the joint claimants`'s `the first person`)

