    `the matter is one that regulations provide is or is not to be taken into account`

-- src:612 | (4) Regulations are to provide for—
-- src:613 | (a) the amount of a reduction under this section;
@ref s 46 JSA 19A(4)(a) (src:612-613)
GIVEN `the award before the reduction, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 46 JSA 19A(4)(a) the award after the reduction, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds`
    WHEN JUST reduction THEN
        BRANCH
            IF reduction AT MOST `the award before the reduction, in pounds`
            THEN JUST (`the award before the reduction, in pounds` MINUS reduction)
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what happens when the reduction is more than the award
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations are to provide for the amount of a reduction"; they are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

